--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

ArenaBench has no bundled third-party code and no Python package
dependencies. It relies at runtime on tools it does not redistribute:

  Harbor  (https://github.com/laude-institute/harbor)
      The benchmark runner. ArenaBench invokes the `harbor` executable and
      imports its agent registry when present. Not vendored.

  Docker
      Task containers, and the optional MP4 recorder sidecar. Not vendored.

  Stella Harbor adapter  (AGPL-3.0-only)
      ArenaBench's Stella contestant subclasses `stella_harbor.StellaAgent`,
      which is part of the Stella project and licensed AGPL-3.0-only. It is
      an OPTIONAL runtime dependency, resolved by import from a path the
      operator supplies. ArenaBench does not vendor, redistribute, or link
      against it at build time, and every other ArenaBench feature works
      without it.

  The recorder container image
      Built on demand from recorder/Dockerfile on the operator's machine. It
      installs Debian packages (xvfb, xterm, ffmpeg, python3, fonts-dejavu)
      under their own licences. ArenaBench distributes the Dockerfile, not
      the image or its contents.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Benchmarks
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Datasets registered with ArenaBench (Terminal-Bench and any others an
operator adds) are the property of their respective authors and carry their
own licences and terms of use. ArenaBench references them by content digest
and does not redistribute task content.
